WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.447
Are you thinking of knitting
a sweater on your knitting machine?

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.210
Stop.

00:00:04.243 --> 00:00:08.207
Before you start, there are a few
things that you need to know.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.240
If you've just bought a knitting machine
and you're dreaming of making your

00:00:11.273 --> 00:00:14.210
first sweater, you're not alone.

00:00:14.243 --> 00:00:15.690
But here's the thing.

00:00:15.723 --> 00:00:19.280
Knitting a sweater on your machine isn't
as simple as just threading up

00:00:19.313 --> 00:00:21.650
some yarn and getting started.

00:00:21.683 --> 00:00:26.050
A lot of knitters jump right into big
projects like sweaters,

00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:30.530
only to run into frustration
when things don't go as planned.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:35.010
Maybe the fit is off,
or the yarn isn't behaving the way you

00:00:35.043 --> 00:00:39.130
expected, or your machine feels
like it has a mind of its own.

00:00:39.163 --> 00:00:40.970
Does that sound familiar?

00:00:41.003 --> 00:00:42.250
You're not alone.

00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:48.410
This is one of the most common struggles
I hear from knitters every day.

00:00:48.443 --> 00:00:52.240
The truth is, knitting a great sweater
takes more than just

00:00:52.273 --> 00:00:53.930
a machine and some yarn.

00:00:53.963 --> 00:00:58.690
It takes planning, skills, and practice.

00:00:58.723 --> 00:01:01.810
A sweater isn't just It's
another small project.

00:01:01.843 --> 00:01:09.290
It's a mix of design, fit, and finishing
techniques that all need to work together.

00:01:09.323 --> 00:01:14.690
If one piece is off, the whole
sweater can be really disappointing.

00:01:14.723 --> 00:01:20.010
But here's the good news: no matter what
your experience level, success is

00:01:20.043 --> 00:01:22.330
absolutely within your reach.

00:01:22.363 --> 00:01:27.490
If you're feeling overwhelmed about
where to start, I've got you covered.

00:01:27.523 --> 00:01:31.880
I've put together a free sweater planning
worksheet to help you think through your

00:01:31.913 --> 00:01:35.850
design, yarn, and the skills you'll need.

00:01:35.883 --> 00:01:40.160
Grab it now, just click the link below
and start your sweater

00:01:40.193 --> 00:01:43.050
journey with confidence.

